'' =====================================================================
'' conflict-testQ-doc-claims-battery.spin2
''
'' WHY THIS EXISTS: six claims are about to be written into the Debug Window
'' Manual on the strength of "v55 and the REF agree" -- and NOTHING ELSE.  That
'' is the exact combination that produced ch04:49 ("outline"), ch04:241
'' ("ignored"), ch04:84 ("garbage"), the LONGS_1BIT packing default, and the FFT
'' MAG inversion.  Every one of them was WRONG.  Two agreeing documents is not
'' evidence.  Settle them on silicon before they ship.
''
'' EVERY WINDOW GETS AN EXPLICIT POS.  SAVE WINDOW / desktop scrapes are
'' occlusion-vulnerable, and PNut has NO auto-layout -- no-POS windows stack at
'' the host origin and the scrapes capture whichever window is on top.  That
'' silently voided an earlier run (gateP_ds03 turned out to be a byte-for-byte
'' crop of gateP_ds04).  Never again.
''
'' EVIDENCE IS FILE-EXISTENCE + IMAGE CONTENT.  No log is required, so this runs
'' identically on PNut (which emits no debug log) and on pnut-term-ts.
''
'' *** USE PLAIN `SAVE ONLY -- NEVER `SAVE WINDOW.  (revised 2026-07-14) ***
''   `SAVE WINDOW is a DESKTOP SCRAPE and it is UNRELIABLE on PNut.  In the first run of
''   this battery, every SAVE WINDOW capture (q2/q4/q5/q6) came back as DESKTOP WALLPAPER
''   -- not a stale frame, not the wrong window: wallpaper.  The same form also returned
''   solid green instead of the SPARSE pattern in conflict-testP, for windows whose plain
''   SAVE showed sparse correctly.
''   A plain `SAVE reads the window's OWN buffer: occlusion-immune, chrome-free, and it
''   worked on every single test that used it.  Note it writes the bitmap at 1x
''   UN-DOTSIZED (v55 L1347 is correct) -- which is FINE here: we are reading COLOURS and
''   PIXEL POSITIONS, not magnified geometry.  (A SPARSE window is the exception: it
''   allocates at physical size, which is why testP's plain saves came out magnified.)
''
'' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
'' Q1  Does a BARE `SAVE` (no filename) write anything?
''       doc says: NO -- silently writes nothing.
''       RAIL : q1_rail.bmp (a normal SAVE) MUST exist -> proves SAVE works here.
''       TEST : if the doc is right, NO extra file appears.
''
'' Q2  Is a keyword after SAVE consumed and DISCARDED?
''       doc says: `Win SAVE CLEAR  writes NO file AND loses the CLEAR.
''       TEST : q2 window is filled GREEN, then sent `SAVE CLEAR .
''              - no q2*.bmp should appear
''              - the window should STILL BE GREEN (the CLEAR was eaten)
''       RAIL : q2b window gets a plain `CLEAR  -> it MUST go black.
''              If q2b does not clear, CLEAR is broken and Q2 is INCONCLUSIVE.
''
'' Q3  Does SAVE write the FRONT buffer (a stale frame under UPDATE mode)?
''       doc says: YES -- you capture the PREVIOUS frame.
''       TEST : q3 is created with UPDATE (buffered).  Fill RED -> `UPDATE (red is
''              now the front buffer).  Fill GREEN but do NOT update.  SAVE.
''              - saved image RED   -> doc right: SAVE captured the STALE frame.
''              - saved image GREEN -> doc WRONG: SAVE captured the live buffer.
''
'' Q4  Does a RUNTIME `RATE -1 freeze BITMAP auto-refresh?
''       doc says: YES -- no -1 substitution outside the create message, and the
''                 rate cycle tests equality against an up-counter, so it never
''                 matches.  (v55's own Feeding table advertises RATE -1 as legal!)
''       TEST : q4 filled GREEN and captured (q4_before).  Then `RATE -1, then fed
''              a full canvas of RED, then captured again (q4_after).
''              - q4_after still GREEN -> doc right: auto-refresh FROZE.
''              - q4_after RED         -> doc WRONG: it kept refreshing.
''       RAIL : q5 does the identical thing with `RATE 6 (a legal positive rate).
''              q5_after MUST be RED.  If it is not, the feed itself is broken and
''              Q4 is INCONCLUSIVE, not a confirmation.
''
'' Q6  Is an out-of-range BITMAP `SET` CLAMPED, or IGNORED?
''       *** THIS ONE REVERSES SHIPPED TEXT.  ch04:241 says "ignored, not clamped." ***
''       doc(REF) says: CLAMPED (KeyValWithin = assign-and-clamp).
''       TEST : q6 canvas is 8x8, cleared BLACK.  `SET 999 999 then plot ONE WHITE
''              pixel.
''              - a white pixel at the BOTTOM-RIGHT corner -> CLAMPED (REF right,
''                the manual is wrong and must be reversed).
''              - no white pixel anywhere               -> IGNORED (the manual is
''                right; do NOT reverse it).
''
'' Q7  Does PLOT `OPACITY 256 wrap to 0 (transparent)?
''       doc says: YES -- assigned into a byte with range-checking off, so 256 -> 0.
''                 The exact inverse of what a reader expects (fully opaque).
''       TEST : q7 draws TWO dots -- LEFT at OPACITY 255, RIGHT at OPACITY 256.
''              - left visible, right INVISIBLE -> doc right: 256 wrapped to 0.
''              - both visible                  -> doc WRONG: 256 clamped to 255.
''       The left dot is the rail: if IT is missing, the drawing is broken.
''
'' Q8  CLOSE: does the rest of the message run FIRST, then the window close?
''       doc says: YES -- update-first, close-second.
''       TEST : `q8 SAVE 'q8_saved' CLOSE   (both in ONE message)
''              - q8_saved.bmp EXISTS *and* the q8 window is GONE -> doc right.
''              - file missing                                    -> CLOSE ran first.
''              - window still open                               -> CLOSE is a no-op.
''       RUN LAST -- it destroys its own window.
'' =====================================================================

CON
  _clkfreq = 100_000_000

PUB main() | i

  '' ---------- Q1 : bare SAVE writes nothing? ----------
  debug(`BITMAP q1 POS 0 0 SIZE 8 8 DOTSIZE 8 RGB24)
  repeat i from 0 to 63
    debug(`q1 `($00FF00))
  waitms(200)
  debug(`q1 save 'q1_rail')            ' RAIL: this file MUST appear
  debug(`q1 save)                      ' TEST: bare SAVE -- expect NO file

  '' ---------- Q2 : is a keyword after SAVE eaten? ----------
  debug(`BITMAP q2 POS 200 0 SIZE 8 8 DOTSIZE 8 RGB24)
  debug(`BITMAP q2b POS 400 0 SIZE 8 8 DOTSIZE 8 RGB24)
  repeat i from 0 to 63
    debug(`q2  `($00FF00))
    debug(`q2b `($00FF00))
  waitms(200)
  debug(`q2 save clear)                ' TEST: expect NO file AND the CLEAR is eaten
  debug(`q2b clear)                    ' RAIL: a plain CLEAR -- q2b MUST go black
  waitms(200)
  debug(`q2  save 'q2_after')   ' expect STILL GREEN (clear was eaten)
  debug(`q2b save 'q2b_rail')   ' expect BLACK

  '' ---------- Q3 : does SAVE write the stale front buffer? ----------
  debug(`BITMAP q3 POS 0 200 SIZE 8 8 DOTSIZE 8 RGB24 UPDATE)
  repeat i from 0 to 63
    debug(`q3 `($FF0000))              ' RED
  debug(`q3 update)                    ' RED is now the front buffer
  waitms(200)
  repeat i from 0 to 63
    debug(`q3 `($00FF00))              ' GREEN -- drawn but NOT updated
  waitms(200)
  debug(`q3 save 'q3_stale')           ' RED => stale (doc right).  GREEN => live.

  '' ---------- Q4/Q5 : does a runtime RATE -1 freeze the display? ----------
  debug(`BITMAP q4 POS 200 200 SIZE 8 8 DOTSIZE 8 RGB24)
  debug(`BITMAP q5 POS 400 200 SIZE 8 8 DOTSIZE 8 RGB24)
  repeat i from 0 to 63
    debug(`q4 `($00FF00))
    debug(`q5 `($00FF00))
  waitms(200)
  debug(`q4 save 'q4_before')   ' GREEN
  debug(`q5 save 'q5_before')   ' GREEN

  debug(`q4 rate -1)                   ' TEST : doc says this FREEZES auto-refresh
  debug(`q5 rate 6)                    ' RAIL : a legal positive rate -- must keep working
  repeat i from 0 to 63
    debug(`q4 `($FF0000))              ' feed RED
    debug(`q5 `($FF0000))              ' feed RED
  waitms(300)
  debug(`q4 save 'q4_after')    ' still GREEN => FROZE (doc right).  RED => not frozen.
  debug(`q5 save 'q5_after')    ' MUST be RED, or Q4 is inconclusive

  '' ---------- Q6 : is an out-of-range SET clamped, or ignored? ----------
  '' *** reverses ch04:241 if CLAMPED ***
  debug(`BITMAP q6 POS 600 200 SIZE 8 8 DOTSIZE 8 RGB24)
  repeat i from 0 to 63
    debug(`q6 `($000000))              ' all black
  waitms(200)
  debug(`q6 set 999 999)               ' far out of range on a 8x8 canvas
  debug(`q6 `($FFFFFF))                ' plot ONE white pixel
  waitms(200)
  debug(`q6 save 'q6_clamp')    ' white at BOTTOM-RIGHT => CLAMPED.  none => IGNORED.

  '' ---------- Q7 : does PLOT OPACITY 256 wrap to 0 (transparent)? ----------
  debug(`PLOT q7 POS 600 0 SIZE 200 100 BACKCOLOR BLACK)
  debug(`q7 WHITE LINESIZE 20)
  debug(`q7 SET 50 50 DOT 20 255)      ' RAIL: opacity 255 -- MUST be visible
  debug(`q7 SET 150 50 DOT 20 256)     ' TEST: 256 -> 0 (invisible) if it wraps
  waitms(200)
  debug(`q7 save 'q7_opacity')

  '' ---------- Q8 : CLOSE -- update first, close second?  (RUN LAST) ----------
  debug(`BITMAP q8 POS 0 400 SIZE 8 8 DOTSIZE 8 RGB24)
  repeat i from 0 to 63
    debug(`q8 `($00FFFF))              ' cyan, so it is unmistakable
  waitms(300)
  debug(`q8 save 'q8_saved' close)     ' file EXISTS + window GONE => update-first
  waitms(500)

  repeat
